 ### [Multiplex Training via S3IM](10894-multiplex-training-via-s3im.md)
-Augments photometric losses with Stochastic Structural SIMilarity (S3IM) to capture non-local structural information, unlike standard SSIM which captures only local information.
+Augments standard photometric losses with a Stochastic Structural SIMilarity (S3IM) term to improve reconstruction quality for complex details and sparse inputs. It distinguishes itself from standard SSIM optimization by capturing non-local structural information from distant pixels across different images via stochastic patching, whereas standard SSIM only captures local structural information from nearby pixels within a single image.
 
 ### [S3IM (Stochastic Structural SIMilarity)](10895-s3im-stochastic-structural-similarity.md)
-A regularization term capturing nonlocal structural similarity by processing pixels as a collective set, enforcing global structural consistency at low computational cost, unlike point-wise MSE losses.
+A regularization term that captures nonlocal structural similarity by processing multiple data points (pixels/rays) as a collective set rather than individually. It addresses the limitation of point-wise losses like MSE, which fail to utilize the collective supervision of distant pixels. Unlike conventional pixel-wise losses, S3IM cannot be expressed as the sum of any loss computed over individual pixels from the batch, allowing it to enforce global structural consistency at nearly no additional computational cost.
 
 ### [Semantic Consistency Loss (CLIP-based)](11955-semantic-consistency-loss-clip-based.md)
-Enforces consistency between rendered and ground-truth image features using a pre-trained CLIP-ViT encoder, addressing ambiguity via discriminative feature matching rather than generative priors.
